      },
      {
        "value": "100000",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "According to Ato Nega there are more than one million Qemant people, of whom 350,000 still speak the language... Qemant is being replaced by Amharic, and there is a tendency for the language to die [Date Of Info: 2002]"
